# Technical Excellence

## Code Changes

- Imports at top of file; no inline imports unless circular dependency is documented.
- TypeScript: exhaustive `switch` with `never` in default for unions/enums.
- Read before write; reuse existing abstractions; comments only for non-obvious logic.
- Add tests only when requested or when they cover meaningful behavior.

## Agent Execution

- Run compile/lint/test after substantive edits.
- Commit focused changes with clear messages; push before PR.
- Use Cloud Agents for long-running tasks; verify locally when possible.

## Verification Skills

- `check-compiler-errors` — after code changes
- `verify-this` — when validating a claim with evidence
- `review-and-ship` — before opening PRs
- `run-smoke-tests` — for UI changes

## PR Quality

- Small, reviewable diffs; descriptive PR body with verification steps.
- No AI slop: remove redundant comments, dead code, and unnecessary abstractions.
